# Motion & scroll

## Rhythm

**SPECTACLE → SILENCE → SPECTACLE → SILENCE.** Not everything animates.

| Tier | Duration | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Micro | 120–220ms | buttons, icons, states |
| Interface | 300–500ms | cards, menus, overlays |
| Cinematic | 600–1100ms / scroll | hero, storytelling |

## Scroll-linked pipeline

`useScroll` → MotionValue → `useTransform` → optional `useSpring` → transform/opacity

- `useSpring` = perceptual smoothing, **not** scroll throttling
- No per-frame React state; no redundant scroll listeners; no artificial throttling unless a non-Motion calc needs it
- Sticky storytelling OK; never hijack/prevent native scroll

## LazyMotion

- Prefer `m` inside LazyMotion trees; do not casually import full `motion` there
- Baseline: `domAnimation`
- `domMax` only for genuine drag/pan/layout needs; never ship globally “just in case”
- Document any isolated chunk that needs a different feature bundle

## Earn idle cost

Pause irrelevant animation work via intersection visibility, document visibility, reduced motion, and responsive gating. No permanent decorative rAF loops. Justify `useAnimationFrame` and pause when offscreen/hidden.

## Signature

- Desktop: laptop CSS 3D + Motion module
- Mobile: separate layer story module — never shrunk laptop
- Reduced-motion: intentional alternate presentation

## content-visibility

Never blind-apply. Especially avoid on active sticky laptop containers unless profiling proves benefit. Reserve for large static below-fold sections.
